      "id": "df57h5h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Constitutional & Administrative Status"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Fifth Schedule governs Scheduled Areas in states other than Assam, Meghalaya, Tripura, and Mizoram, empowering Governors to adapt state laws.",
        "The Panchayats (Extension to Scheduled Areas) Act, 1996 (PESA) extends self-governance to tribal areas by empowering the Gram Sabha.",
        "Tribal Advisory Councils (TAC) consisting of up to 20 members are established in Fifth Schedule states to advise on tribal welfare.",
        "Autonomous District Councils (ADCs) under the Sixth Schedule enjoy extensive legislative, executive, and judicial powers in specific Northeastern states.",
        "Articles 330, 332, and 335 provide constitutional guarantees for representation and affirmative action for Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes."
      ],
      "id": "90w9oyh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xti5z5k"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ffnzzhr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ywlkaac"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "The Gram Sabha shall be competent to safeguard and preserve the traditions and customs of the people, their cultural identity, community resources, and the customary mode of dispute resolution.",
      "id": "56qf7wf"
